output:
Surah 3:134
Arabic (Uthmani): ٱلَّذِينَ يُنفِقُونَ فِى ٱلسَّرَّآءِ وَٱلضَّرَّآءِ وَٱلْكَـٰظِمِينَ ٱلْغَيْظَ وَٱلْعَافِينَ عَنِ ٱلنَّاسِ ۗ وَٱللَّهُ يُحِبُّ ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ
Translation (Saheeh International): Who spend [in the cause of Allāh] during ease and hardship and who restrain anger and who pardon the people - and Allāh loves the doers of good;

Surah 10:105
Arabic (Uthmani): وَأَنْ أَقِمْ وَجْهَكَ لِلدِّينِ حَنِيفًا وَلَا تَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلْمُشْرِكِينَ
Translation (Saheeh International): And [commanded], 'Direct your face [i.e., self] toward the religion, inclining to truth, and never be of those who associate others with Allāh;

Surah 16:106
Arabic (Uthmani): مَن كَفَرَ بِٱللَّهِ مِنۢ بَعْدِ إِيمَـٰنِهِۦٓ إِلَّا مَنْ أُكْرِهَ وَقَلْبُهُۥ مُطْمَئِنٌّۢ بِٱلْإِيمَـٰنِ وَلَـٰكِن مَّن شَرَحَ بِٱلْكُفْرِ صَدْرًا فَعَلَيْهِمْ غَضَبٌ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ
Translation (Saheeh International): Whoever disbelieves in [i.e., denies] Allāh after his belief...1 except for one who is forced [to renounce his religion] while his heart is secure in faith. But those who [willingly] open their breasts to disbelief, upon them is wrath from Allāh, and for them is a great punishment;

Surah 20:106
Arabic (Uthmani): فَيَذَرُهَا قَاعًا صَفْصَفًا
Translation (Saheeh International): And He will leave it [i.e., the earth] a level plain;

Surah 25:65
Arabic (Uthmani): وَٱلَّذِينَ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَا ٱصْرِفْ عَنَّا عَذَابَ جَهَنَّمَ ۖ إِنَّ عَذَابَهَا كَانَ غَرَامًا
Translation (Saheeh International): And those who say, "Our Lord, avert from us the punishment of Hell. Indeed, its punishment is ever adhering;

Surah 37:46
Arabic (Uthmani): بَيْضَآءَ لَذَّةٍ لِّلشَّـٰرِبِينَ
Translation (Saheeh International): White and delicious to the drinkers;

Surah 55:19
Arabic (Uthmani): مَرَجَ ٱلْبَحْرَيْنِ يَلْتَقِيَانِ
Translation (Saheeh International): He released the two seas,1 meeting [one another];

Surah 56:66
Arabic (Uthmani): إِنَّا لَمُغْرَمُونَ
Translation (Saheeh International): [Saying], "Indeed, we are [now] in debt;

Surah 68:26
Arabic (Uthmani): فَلَمَّا رَأَوْهَا قَالُوٓا۟ إِنَّا لَضَآلُّونَ
Translation (Saheeh International): But when they saw it, they said, "Indeed, we are lost;

Surah 69:36
Arabic (Uthmani): وَلَا طَعَامٌ إِلَّا مِنْ غِسْلِينٍ
Translation (Saheeh International): Nor any food except from the discharge of wounds;

Surah 74:21
Arabic (Uthmani): ثُمَّ نَظَرَ
Translation (Saheeh International): Then he considered [again];

Surah 74:22
Arabic (Uthmani): ثُمَّ عَبَسَ وَبَسَرَ
Translation (Saheeh International): Then he frowned and scowled;

Surah 80:11
Arabic (Uthmani): كَلَّآ إِنَّهَا تَذْكِرَةٌ
Translation (Saheeh International): No! Indeed, they [i.e., these verses] are a reminder;

Surah 82:11
Arabic (Uthmani): كِرَامًا كَـٰتِبِينَ
Translation (Saheeh International): Noble and recording;

Surah 84:13
Arabic (Uthmani): إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ فِىٓ أَهْلِهِۦ مَسْرُورًا
Translation (Saheeh International): Indeed, he had [once] been among his people in happiness;

Surah 96:17
Arabic (Uthmani): فَلْيَدْعُ نَادِيَهُۥ
Translation (Saheeh International): Then let him call his associates;
